Bundled third-party source
--------------------------

src/toywasm/ contains part of toywasm, a WebAssembly interpreter by
YAMAMOTO Takashi, vendored from https://github.com/yamt/toywasm at tag
v76.0.0, commit 0462f000e110ad0752de67d9a256727d97c21e2d. toywasm is
distributed under the 2-clause BSD licence, reproduced in full in
inst/TOYWASM_LICENSE.

Copyright (c) 2022-2026 YAMAMOTO Takashi. All rights reserved.

Only the interpreter library (upstream lib/) is included, and only the files
the package's configuration needs. The sources are modified during vendoring
to suit R: assertions can no longer call abort(), one GNU C extension that
warns under -pedantic is replaced by upstream's portable fallback, and an
upstream compile error in a statistics function is fixed. Upstream's logging
and stdio helpers (xlog.c, nbio.c) are replaced by src/toywasm_shim.c, and
the build configuration is src/toywasm_config.h.

tools/vendor-toywasm.sh and tools/vendor/ in the package's source repository
perform the vendoring and record what each change does; VENDORED,
manifest.tsv and checksums.sha256 there record the provenance and let the
tree be verified against it. Those files are development tooling and are not
shipped in this tarball.
